WEBVTT

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:32.018
But today, scholars generally feel

00:04:32.018 --> 00:04:37.106
that modern fanfiction
traces its origins to typewritten zines

00:04:37.106 --> 00:04:40.109
written by “Star Trek” fans
in the ‘60s and’ 70s.

00:04:40.901 --> 00:04:42.987
And with the growth of the internet,

00:04:42.987 --> 00:04:45.448
barriers to sharing
have been lowered further.

00:04:46.282 --> 00:04:49.368
Millions of people are writing
and sharing fan fiction

00:04:49.368 --> 00:04:51.203
on a variety of websites

00:04:51.203 --> 00:04:54.707
around existing plots like “Harry Potter,”

00:04:54.707 --> 00:04:56.000
“Twilight,”

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.543
“Naruto,”

00:04:57.543 --> 00:04:59.045
“My Little Pony” --

00:04:59.045 --> 00:05:00.046
(Laughter)